  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `assets/posts/grblhal.cps` (`onCycle`) and `assets/posts/tormach.cps` (`onCycle`) now emit `\"P\" + secs(dwell)` whenever `g === \"G86\"`.\n- A zero-dwell bore now writes `P0` on every opening `G86` block instead of omitting `P`.\n- Modal `X Y` holes inside an open `grblhal.cps` group still omit `P`, while `tormach.cps` cancels with `G80` on each hop and writes `P0` on each new `G86` block.\n- `G82` and `G89` still require `dwell > 0` for `P`, and zero-dwell `BACKBORE` still emits `G85` without `P`.\n- Recorded the decision in `docs/decisions/2362-g86-zero-dwell.md` (branched from `upstream/main` `4cab68f97`).\n\n## Cause\n\nBoth posts gated the cycle `P` word on `dwell > 0 && (g === \"G82\" || g === \"G86\" || g === \"G89\")`.\nBecause LinuxCNC's `convert_cycle_xy` requires a non-negative `P` word on the first `G86` block after `G80` or at cycle start, and grblHAL follows the LinuxCNC canned-cycle specification, zero-dwell `G86` blocks omitted `P`.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pinning tests in `crates/post/tests/bore_cycle.rs`: `grblhal_zero_dwell_g86_has_p0`, `tormach_zero_dwell_g86_has_p0`, and `canned_posts_write_g86_and_no_other_cycle` all failed before the fix and pass after it (all 9 tests in `bore_cycle` pass).\n- Mutation checks:\n  - Restored `upstream/main` `assets/posts/grblhal.cps` -> `grblhal_zero_dwell_g86_has_p0` failed; restored the fix -> passed.\n  - Restored `upstream/main` `assets/posts/tormach.cps` -> `tormach_zero_dwell_g86_has_p0` failed; restored the fix -> passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 130 of 130 steps passed (90 `camcraft-post` steps and 40 `camcraft-app` steps, wall 3.5 min).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed with no warnings.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\n- `crates/post/tests/golden/bore/grblhal.nc`: line 15 changed `G86 X10 Y10 Z-12 R2 F120` to `G86 X10 Y10 Z-12 R2 P0 F120`.\n- `crates/post/tests/golden/bore/tormach.nc`: lines 19 and 25 changed both `G86` blocks to include `P0`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Physical grblHAL and Tormach PathPilot controller hardware were not run; behavior relies on the LinuxCNC G-code reference and grblHAL's public G-code list.\n- Full `batch` and `release` gates were not run (only `quick` and `clippy`).\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- PR #2346 touches `assets/posts/tormach.cps` (`motionFor` lines already on `upstream/main` via #2386, not the `P`-word guard; touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes).\n- PR #2506 touches `crates/post/tests/bore_cycle.rs` (`EXPANDED` array only; touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes).\n- PR #2515 touches `crates/post/tests/bore_cycle.rs` (doc comment and `SECONDS` array only; touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes).\n\nEffort: high\nChangelog: grblHAL and Tormach posts write P0 on opening G86 bore cycle blocks when dwell is 0\nFixes #2362\n",
